<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE & OFFSET MECHANICS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Calculations &amp; Shifts</div>
    <h2>Understanding the 5-Hour Offset</h2>
    <p>
      To convert Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) to Central Daylight Time (CDT), subtract 5 hours from the standard reference clock:
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>CDT = GMT - 5 Hours</code>
    </p>
    <p>
      Conversely, to convert from Central Daylight Time to Greenwich Mean Time, add 5 hours to the local CDT clock:
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>GMT = CDT + 5 Hours</code>
    </p>
    <p>
      During the summer, the United Kingdom observes British Summer Time (<a href="/gmt-to-bst/">BST, UTC+1</a>), which widens the difference between local UK time and Central US time to 6 hours. However, the foundational difference between the GMT standard (UTC+0) and CDT (UTC−5) strictly remains 5 hours.
    </p>
    <p>
      In winter, North America transitions back to <strong><a href="/gmt-to-cst/">Central Standard Time (CST, UTC−6)</a></strong>, shifting the difference to 6 hours:
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>CST = GMT - 6 Hours</code>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3>Greenwich Mean Time</h3>
      <code>UTC+0 Baseline</code>
      <p>GMT is the solar time standard centered on the Royal Observatory in Greenwich, London. It operates at UTC+0 without daylight saving adjustments.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3>Central Daylight Time</h3>
      <code>UTC-5 Offset</code>
      <p>CDT is active in summer. It advances Central North America clocks by 1 hour relative to standard time to extend evening daylight.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3>Central Standard Time</h3>
      <code>UTC-6 Offset</code>
      <p>CST is active in winter. It represents standard time for Central North America, running 6 hours behind GMT.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

