<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     DATE ROLLOVER & MIDNIGHT CALCULATIONS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="date-rollover" class="reveal">
  <h2>Date Rollover: Converting Between GMT and CDT Across Midnight</h2>
  <p>
    Because Greenwich Mean Time is 5 hours ahead of Central Daylight Time, conversions during late-night or early-morning hours frequently cross calendar day boundaries. Keeping track of the calendar date avoids missed deadlines and scheduling errors:
  </p>

  <div class="content" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <article>
      <h3>Converting GMT to CDT (Early Hours = Previous Day)</h3>
      <p>
        When it is between <strong>00:00 and 04:59 GMT</strong>, local Central Daylight Time falls on the <strong>previous calendar day</strong> (between 19:00 and 23:59 CDT):
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted);">
        <li><strong>00:00 GMT Tuesday (Midnight)</strong> = <strong>19:00 CDT Monday (7:00 PM)</strong> (-1 day)</li>
        <li><strong>02:00 GMT Tuesday</strong> = <strong>21:00 CDT Monday (9:00 PM)</strong> (-1 day)</li>
        <li><strong>04:59 GMT Tuesday</strong> = <strong>23:59 CDT Monday (11:59 PM)</strong> (-1 day)</li>
        <li><strong>05:00 GMT Tuesday</strong> = <strong>00:00 CDT Tuesday (Midnight)</strong> (same calendar day starts)</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Converting CDT to GMT (Late Hours = Next Day)</h3>
      <p>
        When it is between <strong>19:00 and 23:59 CDT</strong> in Central North America, clocks in Greenwich have already rolled over into the <strong>next calendar day</strong> (between 00:00 and 04:59 GMT):
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted);">
        <li><strong>19:00 CDT Monday (7:00 PM)</strong> = <strong>00:00 GMT Tuesday (Midnight)</strong> (+1 day)</li>
        <li><strong>21:00 CDT Monday (9:00 PM)</strong> = <strong>02:00 GMT Tuesday</strong> (+1 day)</li>
        <li><strong>23:30 CDT Monday (11:30 PM)</strong> = <strong>04:30 GMT Tuesday</strong> (+1 day)</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

